        "original_id": "7b605abb-0736-5f0e-9996-537d254ffee5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Exeter House\n- People: Charles Edward Stuart\n- Families: Earls of Exeter\n- Titles: Marquess of Exeter\n- Events: Jacobite Rising of 1745\n- Topics: Peerage of England, Peerage of the United Kingdom\n\nFacts:\n- During the Jacobite Rising of 1745, Charles Edward Stuart stayed at Exeter House.\n- Exeter House was named for the Earls of Exeter, whose family owned the property until 1757.\n- Marquess of Exeter is a title that was created twice, once in the Peerage of England and once in the Peerage of the United Kingdom.",
